# Headlinr — Project Context

## App Identity

- **App name**: Headlinr
- **App package**: `avinash.app.headlinr`
- **News module package**: `avinash.app.news`
- **Min SDK**: 24 | **Target/Compile SDK**: 36
- **Language**: Kotlin | **UI**: Jetpack Compose | **DI**: Hilt

## Architecture

```
GitHub Actions (every 30 min) → Firebase Firestore (article_bundles) → news module (Room SSOT) → app module (UI)
```

- **`news/`** — Data-only library module. Exposes `NewsRepository`, `NewsArticle`, `Category`. No UI, no ViewModel, no Compose.
- **`app/`** — Host app. Owns all screens, ViewModels, navigation, and AdMob. Depends on `:news`.
- Room is the **single source of truth**. All UI reads from Room, never Firestore directly.
- Sync happens only on app open — **no WorkManager**.

## Module Boundaries (strict)

| Layer | Module | Visibility |
|-------|--------|------------|
| `avinash.app.news.api.*` | `news` | PUBLIC — host app imports only this |
| `avinash.app.news.internal.*` | `news` | PRIVATE — never imported by host |
| `avinash.app.headlinr.*` | `app` | Host app code |

