## AdMob Integration

- **App ID**: `ca-app-pub-2136184247126956~9710418457` (in `AndroidManifest.xml` meta-data)
- **Native Ad Unit ID**: `ca-app-pub-2136184247126956/3823812744`
- SDK initialized in `HeadlinrApp.kt` via `MobileAds.initialize()`
- `InFeedAd.kt` loads native ads via `AdLoader`, renders with `NativeAdView`, only shows after `onAdLoaded`
- Ads inserted at random positions (every 5-8 articles) in HomeScreen's `LazyColumn`
- All ad events logged with Timber tag `AdMob` (requested/loaded/failed/impression/click/destroyed + running stats)

## Conventions

- All timestamps stored as `Long` (epoch millis) in Room; `ts` field in `article_bundles` is also epoch millis.
- Article IDs are SHA-256 hashes of `(normalized_title + normalized_source)` — generated by GitHub Actions.
- Categories are **hardcoded locally** in `LocalCategories.kt` (versioned, re-seeded on upgrade) — never fetched from Firebase.
- 7 merged category short codes: `nat` (दुनिया), `spt` (खेल), `ent` (मनोरंजन), `bus` (व्यापार), `tec` (तकनीक), `hlt` (स्वास्थ्य), `edu` (शिक्षा)
- Legacy codes still in DB articles: `pol`, `cri` → queried via nat expansion; `stk` → bus; `sci` → tec
- Category expansion in `NewsRepositoryImpl`: nat→(nat,pol,cri), bus→(bus,stk), tec→(tec,sci)
- International/world/defense categories removed — Indian RSS feeds cover all relevant news under `nat`
- Firebase articles stored as bundles of ≤50 per document (`article_bundles` collection, short field names).
- Zero cost — everything must stay within free tier limits (Firebase Spark, GitHub Actions 2000 min/month, API free tiers).

## GitHub Actions

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `.github/workflows/fetch-news.yml` | Cron workflow, runs every 30 min, uploads article bundles |
| `.github/workflows/cleanup-firebase.yml` | One-time manual trigger, deletes legacy Firebase collections |
| `scripts/fetch_news.py` | Fetches from 29 Hindi RSS feeds from 12 sources (API providers disabled), bundles, uploads to Firebase |
| `scripts/cleanup_firebase.py` | Batch-deletes `news_articles`, `categories`, `rss_metrics` |
| `scripts/requirements.txt` | Python deps for the workflow |

Secrets required in GitHub repo: `FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT` (entire JSON). API keys (`CURRENTSAPI_KEY`, `NEWSDATA_KEY`, `RAPIDAPI_KEY`) no longer used but may still exist in repo secrets.

Single schedule — every 30 min, 29 RSS feeds from 12 sources (API providers disabled in code).

